        <body>
            <div xml:id="d589">

                <pb facs="0720" n="660" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg660"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Lord Gough</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-19"><hi rendition="#italic">July 19,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 157.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: In view of a letter from the Secretary
                    of the Treasury of the 18th instant, I have the honor to request that I may be
                    furnished, for his use, with a list of the sealing vessels of the British
                    Columbia sealing fleet to which were given special licenses during the years
                    1894 and 1895.</p>
                <p>Asking that this matter may be expedited as far as lies in your power to do so, I
                    have the honer, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
